hey everybody i'm fair and cousins in  for david pakman and this is the david  pakman show we've got all kinds of great  stuff coming up today the latest on  afghanistan of course some covet updates  for you and  even a little bit of insight  into what is happening with republican  congressman matt gates and that  investigation and  some other problems that he's having  right here where i'm sitting in  florida's first congressional district  but let's kick things off obviously  still the biggest news in the world  right now  afghanistan  things uh getting worse of course  and here's something interesting that's  happened and this was actually pointed  out by dave weigel  of the washington post where weigel  pointed out over the weekend  that a web page on the rnc's official  website seems to have disappeared  and that website or web page i guess  was the page talking about donald  trump's historic peace deal as they  called it  with the taliban with regards to  afghanistan if you go to that page now  there's just a 404 page not found error  because apparently the republican  national committee doesn't want people  seeing that they're promoting that  ridiculous peace deal that donald trump  allegedly worked out  and there's a couple reasons for that  too so let's dive right into those first  and foremost they don't want any  attention  on what donald trump did as president  with regard to afghanistan and let's be  honest there's a lot  but the peace deal that he allegedly had  worked out with the taliban that was  signed in february of 2020  is the biggest thing they don't want  people to remember  and that's because once you dig down  into the details of this so-called peace  deal you realize how horrible it  actually was and the biggest uh problem  with this peace deal  is that it completely excluded  the afghan government  no leaders from afghanistan were  involved in the drafting of this  and the protections that the united  states agreed to with the taliban did  not extend  to the actual afghanistan  government  the deal only pertained  to u.s troops  and our nato allies in the country that  the taliban  would not attack them in exchange for  the united states agreeing to leave the  country  within 14 months but nowhere  not any part of that agreement did the  taliban say oh by the way we we won't  promise  to not attack the afghanistan government  apparently that was just a major  oversight  of this peace deal  and of course  as soon as the united states leaves  the taliban goes and overthrows the  government of afghanistan  so yeah it's not surprising that they  would want that web page removed from  existence  because they're boasting about it  talking about look what donald trump did  bringing peace to the middle east  with this historic deal  nope  nope another total failure by donald  trump  another reason though that they do not  want this page out there in existence  and i think this is probably the bigger  one  is because they want all the focus right  now  to be on joe biden  that is the goal  make this biden's failure  make this all about his decision  to remove trump's from afghan troops  from afghanistan ignoring the fact that  even just a couple months ago donald  trump was you know screaming at the top  of his lungs  to tell joe biden to get the troops out  of afghanistan  but they have to frame this  as biden's failure because that's the  new talking point  it emerged fast it emerged quick and  based on what we're seeing in the media  tends to be the uh sticking narrative at  this point that this is all joe biden's  fault  and let's obviously be clear about this  that's not the case  this is the fault of four different  administrations  but if you had to lay the blame at  anybody's feet that blame is going to be  squarely at the feet of george w bush  and i will get more into that in just a  little bit but the talking point  from the rnc  from republican officials  from elected officials from donald trump  himself is all about joe biden being a  catastrophic failure  and they're hoping that they can ride  this all the way through the midterms  you know i pointed out yesterday on the  program  that the republicans have had a hell of  a time getting any kind of talking point  to stick about joe biden  they have crafted all these narratives  fox news has tested them out and even  fox news at one point was getting  frustrated because nothing they were  saying or using to attack biden was  resonating with the audience  well this is something that would  resonate  and again as i mentioned fair or not  biden was the president when this  happened so if people are going to blame  somebody they are going to blame him  i don't agree with that assessment at  all  but i also live in reality i've been  doing this long enough you know coming  up on two decades at this point we know  how these things play out  we know where the blame is going to go  and we know the talking points that the  republicans are going to use  and one of the main reasons we know that  is because we're literally already  seeing it happen  on social media in the corporate media  republicans are pushing this non-stop  and they want to keep it that way  they want the focus  to remain on joe biden because that's  the message joe biden  couldn't keep afghanistan safe and if he  can't keep them safe how's he going to  keep you safe  we're already  starting to see the narrative crop up  of oh what does taliban taking over  afghanistan mean for terror attacks here  in the united states  several outlets started reporting  stories like that on monday  they're already trying to pose this as  what is the significant threat that this  will pose to us here in the united  states can biden even keep us safe now  we're right back into that same post 911  mentality  where every time you turn around there's  a boogeyman being pushed on you  by these politicians who are using it  to scare you into submission to scare  you into voting for them  and that's what we're starting to see  now it's disgusting but again it's 100  percent  predictable  this is how they operate this is the way  they craft their narrative this is the  way they sell it to the public  and unfortunately the republican party  is very very good  at selling these narratives in a way  that the democratic party can only ever  dream of being  on issue after issue republicans get out  front on the messaging and that is what  sticks and then the democrats have to  come from behind trying to defend it  debunk it refute it whatever it and  they're never on the offensive and this  narrative has already been lost  it's already been lost  so again  whether you agree with biden's decision  to pull the troops out i do  whether you disagree with it doesn't  matter  the narrative that the media has already  captured is that this is a failure of  the biden administration and republicans  are going to ride that all the way to  the 2022  midterms  i've struggled falling asleep at night  and realized part of it could be because  of the blue light coming from my phone  and computer screens and peer-reviewed  studies have shown that blue light can  suppress the hormone melatonin which can  make it difficult to fall asleep blue  light can disturb your circadian rhythms  but it hasn't been an issue for me since  i discovered blue blocks glasses which  filter out that blue light they're one  of our sponsors a lot of other companies  are mass producing supposed blue light  glasses and factories with no actual  quality standards blue blocks glasses  are made in actual optics labs at their  headquarters in australia they have over  40 stylish frames a prescription version  non-prescription even reading glasses  and for every pair of glasses that blue  blocks sells they give a pair of reading  glasses to someone in need you'll get  twenty percent off when you go to blue  blocks dot com slash pacman the link is  right underneath this video and there's